    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/115": {
      "title": "Admission Counselor",
      "description": "Admission Counselor. Department: Admissions. Full-Time. McMurry University seeks an energetic, relationship-focused Admission Counselor to serve as one of the University's primary recruitment representatives. Admission Counselors will develop and maintain strategic relationships with high schools, community organizations, churches, counselors, alumni, and prospective students while managing a recruitment territory designed to increase enrollment and enhance McMurry University's visibility. This position serves as the face of McMurry University within a specific territory and is responsible for cultivating prospective students from inquiry through enrollment. Travel Required: 4-6 weeks of travel throughout Texas in the Fall and an additional 1-2 weeks in assigned territory in the Spring. Essential Responsibilities: Territory Management & Recruitment Develop and execute a comprehensive territory recruitment plan for assigned territory Build and maintain relationships with high school counselors, administrators, teachers, coaches, and community leaders. Attend high school visits, college fairs, transfer fairs, and community events. Identify opportunities to increase awareness and enrollment within territory Maintain regular communication with prospective students and families. Student Recruitment & Enrollment Counsel prospective students and families regarding admissions requirements, academic programs, scholarships, financial aid, campus life, and the enrollment process. Manage a recruitment funnel from inquiry through enrollment. Conduct individual appointments, virtual meetings, and group presentations. Follow up with prospective students through phone, text, email, and CRM campaigns. Assist students in completing admissions and financial aid requirements. Relationship Development Develop partnerships with high schools, community colleges, churches, homeschool organizations, and community groups. Engage McMurry alumni and supporters within the assigned territory to support recruitment efforts. Partner with coaches, faculty, and university representatives when appropriate. Event Support Assist with planning and execution of: Preview Events Admitted Student Days Campus Visit Programs Special Enrollment Events SOAR - support the execution of Student Orientation and Registration between June and August. Data & Reporting Maintain accurate records within the University's CRM system. Track recruitment activity and enrollment outcomes. Analyze territory trends and recommend strategies for improvement. Submit regular reports regarding territory performance and recruitment efforts. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Valid driver's license and ability to travel throughout Texas. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills. Strong organizational and time management abilities. Ability to work independently while contributing to a collaborative admissions team. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and CRM technology. Preferred Qualifications Previous admissions, enrollment management, recruitment, sales, marketing, or relationship-management experience. Experience in higher education. Familiarity with CRM systems such as Slate, Jenzabar, or similar platforms. Experience conducting presentations and public speaking. Bilingual in English/Spanish is highly preferred Physical Requirements Ability to travel frequently throughout assigned territory. Ability to transport recruitment materials and displays. Ability to stand for extended periods at recruitment events and college fairs. Core Competencies Relationship Building Customer Service Communication Initiative Strategic Thinking Organization Recruitment and Sales Skills Data-Informed Decision Making EEO Statement: McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/81": {
      "title": "Regional Admission Counselor (Dallas-Fort Worth Region)",
      "description": "Regional Admission Counselor (Dallas-Fort Worth Region). Department: Admissions. Full-Time. McMurry University seeks an energetic, relationship-focused Regional Admission Counselor to serve as the University's primary recruitment representative in the Dallas-Fort Worth region. The Regional Admission Counselor will develop and maintain strategic relationships with high schools, community organizations, churches, counselors, alumni, and prospective students while managing a recruitment territory designed to increase enrollment and enhance McMurry University's visibility. This position serves as the face of McMurry University within the DFW market and is responsible for cultivating prospective students from inquiry through enrollment. Travel Required: Extensive regional travel throughout the Dallas-Fort Worth area and periodic travel through other areas in Texas and to McMurry University for university events. Essential Responsibilities: Territory Management & Recruitment Develop and execute a comprehensive territory recruitment plan for assigned DFW counties. Build and maintain relationships with high school counselors, administrators, teachers, coaches, and community leaders. Conduct and/or attend at minimum 3 high school visits, college fairs, transfer fairs, and community events per week during the school year. Identify opportunities to increase awareness and enrollment within assigned markets. Maintain regular communication with prospective students and families. Maintain membership in DARN (DFW Admissions Regional Network) Student Recruitment & Enrollment Counsel prospective students and families regarding admissions requirements, academic programs, scholarships, financial aid, campus life, and the enrollment process. Manage a recruitment funnel from inquiry through enrollment. Conduct individual appointments, virtual meetings, and group presentations. Follow up with prospective students through phone, text, email, and CRM campaigns. Assist 