    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/117": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant. Department: Enrollment Management Administration. Full-Time. The Administrative Assistant provides comprehensive administrative support to the Vice President of Enrollment Management. This position ensures smooth day-to-day operations of the Enrollment Management office, supporting initiatives related to student recruitment, application processing, and overall enrollment goals. The role requires professionalism, discretion, and strong organizational abilities. Major/Essential Duties of the Job: Administrative Support: Manage the VP’s calendar, schedule meetings, and coordinate travel logistics. Draft, edit, and prepare reports, presentations, and official communications. Organize and maintain digital and paper records and files. Process invoices, purchase orders, and track departmental budgets. Operational Support: Serve as a liaison between the VP and internal/external stakeholders. Assist in the preparation and coordination of admissions events and meetings. Maintain up-to-date contact lists and communication flows with prospective students, staff, and external partners. Monitor and ensure timely follow-up on deadlines, projects, and initiatives. Communication & Collaboration: Field calls and email inquiries on behalf of the VP. Prepare briefing materials for meetings and presentations. Support cross-departmental initiatives by coordinating meetings and sharing updates. Assist in compiling enrollment data and updating internal dashboards. Preferred Education/Experience Required: Associate’s degree or equivalent administrative experience. 2+ years in a professional administrative or office support role. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and scheduling tools (e.g., Outlook, Teams). Excellent communication, time management, and multitasking skills. Preferred: Bachelor’s degree. Experience in higher education or student services. Familiarity with CRM systems Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/51": {
      "title": "Dual Credit Adjunct",
      "description": "Dual Credit Adjunct. Department: Enrollment Management Administration. Full-Time. Position Summary The Dual Credit Adjunct Instructor is responsible for delivering high-quality college-level instruction to eligible high school students enrolled in dual credit courses. This position supports student success by maintaining rigorous academic standards, fostering engagement, and ensuring alignment with institutional curriculum and accreditation requirements. Courses may be taught on a high school campus, college campus, online, or in a hybrid format. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teach assigned dual credit courses in accordance with approved college curriculum, syllabi, learning outcomes, and academic policies. Maintain appropriate academic rigor consistent with college-level expectations. Develop and deliver engaging instruction that promotes student learning and success. Evaluate student performance through assignments, exams, projects, and participation. Submit grades, attendance, and required reports in a timely manner. Maintain regular communication with students, high school partners, department leadership, and college administration as needed. Utilize the institution’s learning management system and instructional technologies. Adhere to all institutional policies, FERPA requirements, and applicable state/federal regulations. Participate in orientation, training, and meetings as requested. Support student retention, persistence, and academic integrity. Maintain required credentials and documentation for accreditation compliance. Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in the teaching discipline or a master’s degree with at least 18 graduate semester hours in the teaching discipline. Demonstrated subject matter expertise. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively with high school students, parents, faculty, and school district personnel. Commitment to student success and academic excellence. Ability to use instructional technology and learning management systems. Preferred Qualifications Prior college-level teaching experience. Experience teaching dual credit or early college students. Online teaching experience. Familiarity with SACSCOC or other regional accreditation faculty credentialing standards. Secondary education teaching experience or partnership experience with school districts. Work Environment Courses may be taught at partner high schools, on campus, or online. Evening or daytime teaching assignments may be available depending on scheduling needs. Travel to partner sites may be required. Physical Requirements Ability to communicate effectively in classroom and virtual settings. Ability to sit or stand for extended periods during instruction. Ability to operate standard classroom and computer equipment. Compensation Compensation is based on course load, credentials, experience, and institutional adjunct pay schedules. Additional Information Adjunct appointments are part-time, term-based, and contingent upon enrollment, program needs, and successful completion of credentialing requirements. Equal Opportunity Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/112": {
      "title": "Facilities Maintenance Technician Electrician",
      "description": "Facilities Maintenance Technician Electrician. Department: Facilities & Maintenance. Full-Time. Major/Essential Duties of the Job: • Performs a variety of technical and skilled work involved in the installation, maintenance, preventative maintenance, and repair of electrical wiring, and equipment. • Works with and around low to high voltage; 12 volt AC/DC up to 3 phase 480 volt. • Basic troubleshooting methods for electrical circuits. • Works with conduits, wires, pull boxes, switch boxes and switches. • Observes and reports discrepancies. • Discusses tasks and projects and suggests appropriate methods for completion. • Submits work order completion reports completely, timely, and accurately. • Operates vehicles, equipment, and hand/power tools as necessary. • Cares for and maintains tools, equipment, keys, uniforms, and other items issued. • Assists other personnel as directed. • Performs other duties as assigned. Required Education/Experience: High school graduate or GED. Basic knowledge and experience working with electricity. Ability to diagnose problems and determine proper repair procedures. Experience with hand and power tools. Knowledge of basic safety requirements, procedures, and techniques. Ability and willingness to learn new skills, knowledge, and techniques. Preferred Education/Experience: Trade school graduate. Journeyman or Master's License preferred EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/109": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician. Department: Facilities & Maintenance. Full-Time. McMurry University is seeking a dependable and skilled Maintenance Technician to support campus operations by performing routine and preventive maintenance, repairs, and general facility upkeep across all university buildings and grounds. The ideal candidate will have a broad skill set in carpentry, plumbing, HVAC , electrical, and mechanical systems and a strong commitment to maintaining a safe, functional, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Job Duties: Performs all aspects of plumbing from repairs to installation new equipment Perform paint, sheetrock, & carpentry repairs on any and all systems and facilities on University-owned property. Basic troubleshooting for electrical circuits. Observes and reports discrepancies. Discusses tasks and projects and suggests appropriate methods for completion. Submits work order completion reports completely, timely, and accurately. Operates vehicles, equipment, and hand/power tools as necessary. Maintains and cleans tools and equipment used in daily activities. Cares for and maintains tools, equipment, keys, uniforms, and other items issued. Assists other personnel as directed. Cleans tools, equipment, and work areas as directed. Performs other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: High school graduate or GED. Knowledge of plumbing repairs, and installation of plumbing equipment. General knowledge of paint, sheetrock repair, and carpentry. Experience with hand and power tools. Knowledge of basic safety requirements, procedures, and techniques. Ability and willingness to learn new skills, knowledge, and techniques. Preferred Qualifications: Trade school graduate Minimum Required Education: High School/G.E.D. Physical Demands: This position is very active and requires standing, walking, bending, kneeling, stooping, crouching, crawling, and climbing during the day. The employee must frequently lift and/or move items over 50 pounds. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/116": {
      "title": "Vice President of Finance",
      "description": "Vice President of Finance. Department: Finance. Full-Time. Position Summary The Vice President for Finance and Administration serves as McMurry University’s Chief Financial Officer, providing strategic leadership and oversight of the university’s financial health and administrative operations. Reporting directly to the President and serving as a key member of the President’s Cabinet, this role supports the institution's mission, vision, and strategic goals by ensuring fiscal integrity, operational efficiency, and a robust infrastructure to support the university community. Major/Essential Duties: Financial Leadership Lead all financial operations, including budgeting, financial reporting, investment management, and long-term financial planning. Collaborate with the Board of Trustees’ Finance, Endowment, and Audit Committees to establish financial goals and strategies. Develop, monitor, and report on the university’s annual operating and capital budgets, ensuring alignment with strategic objectives. Oversee the management and performance of the university’s invested financial assets in partnership with the Endowment Committee. Foster collaborative relationships with external financial advisors, including auditors, investment managers, and banking institutions. Provide transparent, data-driven financial insights to stakeholders, including senior leadership, faculty, and staff. Administrative Leadership Supervise key leadership roles, such as the Controller Accountants and Grant Accountants. Develop and implement long-term campus master planning, property acquisition, and infrastructure development strategies. Ensure compliance with all applicable federal, state, and institutional regulations and standards. Institutional Leadership Serve as a trusted advisor to the President and Cabinet on resource allocation and operational strategies to achieve institutional goals. Represent the university in interactions with external stakeholders, including auditors, legal advisors, and government agencies. Provide leadership for Board of Trustees presentations and updates, including preparation for committee meetings. Fund Accounting & Capital Planning: Deep technical knowledge of multi-fund accounting (GAAP). They must understand how to manage restricted vs. unrestricted funding and oversee long-term capital bonds or campus facility debt infrastructure. Enterprise ERP Management: Practical experience overseeing or upgrading complex Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) systems (such as Jenzabar, Banner, or Workday) and utilizing data visualization tools for campus-wide forecasting. Relational Leadership & Shared Governance Mission Alignment: Private, faith-based institutions require leaders who support the university's holistic mission, viewing financial health as a means to enhance student persistence and success. Collaborative Change Management: The capacity to break down silos and communicate transparently with academic deans, faculty senates, and student affairs. They must be able to translate complex financial realities into accessible narratives for non-financial campus stakeholders Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field from an accredited institution. CPA certification (active licensure). Minimum of 10 years of progressive leadership experience in financial operations, with at least five years in higher education or a comparable non-profit setting. Strong understanding of GAAP, FASB standards, and endowment management principles. Preferred Qualifications Advanced degree in Business Administration, Finance, or a related field. Proven track record of leading successful strategic planning and financial initiatives in a complex organization. Experience with enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems and financial technologies. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Expertise in financial forecasting, budget management, and compliance reporting. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate across diverse constituencies. Strategic thinker with the ability to analyze complex financial data and provide actionable recommendations. Demonstrated ability to lead and inspire teams, fostering a culture of accountability and innovation. Familiarity with the unique financial and operational challenges facing higher education institutions. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/74": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor. Department: Financial Aid. Full-Time. The Division of Student Financial Services seeks a Financial Aid Counselor who is able to work within an established framework for financial services in support of student recruitment, enrollment, retention and graduation goals. Job Duties: Counsel student applicants and parents on matters concerning financial aid packages. Evaluate student problems and requests regarding financial aid awards, and take appropriate action. Advise students regarding financial eligibility, aid programs, planning, budgeting, and debt management. Maintain currency in financial aid packaging, state and federal regulations related to financial aid and University policies and procedures. Maintain communication with students through University channels of email, text messaging, social media, and on-campus advertising. Counsel students in necessary documentation to complete verification and awards. Create and update financial aid forms and multi-media that encourages knowledge of, respect for, and ability to engage diverse student populations. Assist in improving initial award packages and information relevant for students and parents. Perform other job related duties as assigned Required Qualifications: High school diploma and college hours towards a degree. A combination of two years of experience in student financial aid, student services, student personnel, customer service, or related experience. Must have superior communication, customer service, and time management skills as well as a professional demeanor. Candidate must be willing to work evenings and/or weekends during peak, high-volume periods. Candidate must be able to organize, prioritize multiple tasks, meet deadlines, stay on task and manage the work load with efficiency and quality within a highly computerized environment. Must have the ability to use tact, discretion and diplomacy in advising and responding to questions and concerns from students and their families. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. Proficiency with software including MS Word and Excel. Knowledge of state and federal aid programs. Experience in a higher education Financial Aid environment and familiar with Financial Aid software such as PowerFAIDs and Jenzabar. Prior experience making presentations to groups of various sizes. Fluency in English & Spanish, both written and verbal communications is preferred. Minimum Required Education: Some college hours. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/111": {
      "title": "Work Study - Fall '26 - Women's Flag Football Student Assistant",
      "description": "Work Study - Fall '26 - Women's Flag Football Student Assistant. Department: Flag Football. Part-Time. Position Summary: The Women's Flag Football Student Assistant will support the day-to-day operations of the Women's Flag Football program. Responsibilities include assisting with practice and game-day operations, helping with recruiting visit preparations, managing team equipment and uniforms, supporting camps and special events, and assisting with general administrative and organizational tasks. This position will provide great firsthand experience working within a collegiate athletics program while supporting the overall student-athlete experience. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Assist with practice setup and breakdown. Support game-day preparations and operations. Assist with recruiting visits and special events. Assist with organizing, distribute, and inventory of team equipment and uniforms. Assist with camps, and community engagement events. Assist with print, organize, and distribute team materials and documents when needed. Qualifications: Strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends for events. Interest in athletics, sports management, business, marketing, or a related field preferred. Ability to work independently and as part of the team(family). EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/38": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Pool",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Pool. Department: Human Resources. Part-Time. Position Summary McMurry University invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to support instructional needs across academic programs. This posting is used to build a pool of qualified candidates for part-time, temporary teaching assignments as they become available. Appointments are made on a course-by-course basis and are dependent upon departmental needs, enrollment, and funding. Adjunct faculty members play a vital role in delivering high-quality instruction and supporting student success. Selected candidates may teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in their area of expertise, either in-person, online, or hybrid formats. Key Areas of interest (but not limited to): Chemistry Business History Political Science Key Responsibilities Teach assigned courses in alignment with approved curriculum and learning outcomes Prepare course materials, syllabi, and instructional content Engage students through effective teaching strategies and timely communication Assess student learning and provide meaningful feedback Maintain accurate records of attendance, grades, and course activities Adhere to university policies and academic standards Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in the teaching discipline or a related field (minimum 18 graduate hours in the discipline) Relevant professional or teaching experience Strong communication and organizational skills Preferred Qualifications Prior college-level teaching experience Experience with online or hybrid instruction Terminal degree in the discipline (where applicable) Application Requirements Completed application Curriculum Vitae (CV) or resume Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) Additional Information This is a continuous posting used to establish a pool of qualified applicants Applications are reviewed on an as-needed basis Submission of an application does not guarantee employment Adjunct faculty are hired on a per-course, part-time basis Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/108": {
      "title": "Digital Media Specialist",
      "description": "Digital Media Specialist. Department: Marketing & Communications. Full-Time. Position Summary The Digital Media Specialist is a creative and data-informed communications professional responsible for leading the University’s social media strategy and digital storytelling efforts. This role enhances McMurry’s brand presence, supports enrollment and engagement goals, and connects with key audiences through compelling, platform-specific content. Reporting to the Director of Integrated Communications, the Specialist serves as the University’s primary social media strategist and content creator. The position collaborates closely with all members of the StratCom team to support integrated digital campaigns, ensuring messaging is cohesive, engaging, and aligned with institutional priorities. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Social Media Strategy & Management Lead the development and execution of a comprehensive social media strategy aligned with University goals and brand standards. Manage and grow McMurry’s primary social media channels, ensuring consistent voice, tone, and visual identity. Plan and execute an annual and ongoing social content calendar across platforms. Expand audience reach and engagement through strategic content development and active community management. Advise campus partners on social media best practices, account creation, and platform use. Content Creation & Storytelling Create engaging, platform-specific content , including posts, photography, graphics, and short-form video , that highlights the McMurry experience. Capture and produce high-quality photo and video content, including event coverage, interviews, and campus life, and edit short-form video optimized for social platforms. Collaborate with campus partners to identify and develop compelling stories that showcase student life, academic excellence, and campus culture . E nsu re all content aligns with University brand guidelines and editorial standards. Campaign Development & Collaboration Develop and execute social media campaigns that support enrollment, advancement, and institutional initiatives. Collaborate with web and email marketing team members to support integrated, multi-channel campaigns. Provide content, messaging, and creative assets to support website and email marketing initiatives. Coordinate with internal stakeholders and external vendors to support campaign execution. Analytics & Optimization Monitor and analyze social media performance, using data to inform strategy and improve outcomes. Track key performance indicators (KPIs) including engagement, reach, and conversions. Provide regular reports and insights to internal stakeholders. Identify opportunities to optimize content and audience engagement across platforms. Core Competencies Social Media Strategy & Execution Content Creation & Storytelling Data Analysis & Performance Optimization Collaboration & Relationship Building Brand Stewardship Organizational Agility & Adaptability Judgment & Decision-Making Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in marketing , c ommunications, or related field 1–3 years of professional experience in social media or digital content creation Demonstrated experience managing social media platforms and executing campaigns Strong writing , editing, and visual storytelling skills Familiarity with social media management and analytics tools Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education marketing or communications Experience managing social media for an organization or brand Experience analyzing metrics and translating data into actionable insights Basic photography and video editing skills Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/107": {
      "title": "Postal Clerk - Part Time",
      "description": "Postal Clerk - Part Time. Department: Post Office. Part-Time. Major/Essential Duties of the Job: Sign for all accountable mail. Sort and distribute all mail including campus mail. Write notification cards and get signatures for all packages. Sell stamps, money orders, etc. and assist customers as needed. Weigh and meter all outgoing mail. Charge departments for postage used & run daily postage report. Maintain accurate stamp inventory. Issue post office boxes to students and maintain filing records for post office boxes currently in use. Follow USPS Dangerous Goods and Export Compliance safety regulations. Separate and forward mail as necessary. Return mail & forward mail in accordance with USPS regulations. Run bulk mailings. Complete daily financial report (Form 1412-B) as required by USPS and deposit into USPS bank account when required. Pick up mail at the Southern Hills branch Post Office when assigned. Occasional duties: Temporary forwarding of mail in summer months. Cover Print Shop as needed. Other miscellaneous duties as assigned by Post Office Supervisor and/or Vice President of Information & Support Services. Required Education/Experience: High School Diploma/GED Basic computer skills required. Other Job requirements: Must be able to do some lifting, able to multi-task, and detail oriented. Preferred Education/Experience: At least one year of customer service experience desired or previous mail room experience. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/79": {
      "title": "Chapel Band Worship Leader",
      "description": "Chapel Band Worship Leader. Department: Religious Life. Part-Time. Reporting to the Director of Religious & Spiritual Life, the Chapel Band Worship Leader will provide musical and spiritual leadership for McMurry University’s Chapel services. This role focuses on fostering a worshipful environment that enhances the spiritual life of the campus community. The Worship Leader will oversee the planning, preparation, and delivery of worship music in collaboration with the University Chaplains and student musicians. Part-Time (6-8 Hours per Week) | 10 Month Contract (Mid-August through Mid-May) Duties & Responsibilities : Chapel Band Worship Leader will take primary responsibility for the following: Coordinate & Lead Weekly Chapel Band Rehearsal Lead student musicians in planning & preparing music for Chapel Lead rehearsal, including support of student musicians in Chapel Band to develop student leadership through both musical and spiritual growth Recruit, welcome, and integrate new student musicians into Chapel Band in coordination with Religious & Spiritual Life Staff Coordinate setup of portable sound system and necessary equipment during or prior to rehearsal Plan & Lead Worship Music for Weekly Chapel Services (Tuesdays, 11am – 12pm) Lead brief sound check with student musicians prior to start of Chapel Lead Chapel Band in facilitating all music for weekly Chapel services Coordinate tear-down and storage of portable sound system and necessary equipment after Chapel Administrative Support of Chapel Band Prepare & distribute chord charts, lyric sheets, videos/audio files, etc. as needed to support student musicians (using Song Select platform) Input song selections into Planning Center Services Coordinate with RSL Student Worker for preparation of lyric slides (using ProPresenter software) Maintain, organize, and advise on purchasing of instruments, cables, and sound equipment as needed to support the ministry of Chapel Band Meet periodically with Religious & Spiritual Life Staff for planning of Chapel Services Coordinate CCLI Reporting with Religious & Spiritual Life Admin Assistant Special Chapel Worship Opportunities Organize Chapel Band in preparing to lead special worship opportunities throughout the year, including services such as Welcome Week Chapel, Family Weekend Chapel, Final Ala Cumba Memorial Service (Homecoming), Night of Worship, or other opportunities as may arise Organize Chapel Band in preparing to lead special worship opportunities throughout the year outside of campus, such as “McMurry Sundays” at local congregations, Youth Camps, Conferences, or other settings where Chapel Band is invited to lead worship as ambassadors from McMurry University Required Qualifications : Experience in worship leading and music ministry Strong interpersonal and communication skills to effectively mentor and collaborate with students Ability to organize and lead rehearsals efficiently Commitment to fostering a welcoming and inclusive worship environment Flexibility and creativity in adapting to the needs of a diverse campus community Minimum Education Requirements : Some College Hours Preferred Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree in Music, Worship Studies, or related field"
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/102": {
      "title": "Academic Success Coach",
      "description": "Academic Success Coach. Department: S3C. Full-Time. Job Summary This individual will work in support of the Warhawk Success Center (WHSC) to provide direct services to students. The Academic Coach helps students develop skills, behaviors and habits that contribute to success in college. These includes academic and career goal setting, learning strategies, time management and organization, self-regulation and self-efficacy. Job Duties and Responsibilities Fosters persistence and completion of a caseload of students Monitors progress of students in caseload with check-ins, scheduled meetings or proactive outreach and communication, responding to students questions, concerns and needs Conducts academic coaching through individual or group sessions that help students assess their own performance and develop academic success plans Assists students in developing self-efficacy by identifying and overcoming obstacles that may be impeding academic success; works with students to learn strong time management and organization skills; motivates students to practice self-regulation and take ownership of their academic success Helps students in identifying, developing and implementing learning strategies and study skills specific to course materials Refers students to appropriate academic personnel and support resources and collaborates with others to monitor and accelerate the academic progress of the students referred Performs duties that are unique to specific department or academic college Evaluate the academic progress of students completing the Academic Success Plan Maintain appropriate documentation of all meetings with students Maintain regular communication with students throughout the semester Conduct during-term and end-of-term student interventions as needed based on course performance and/or GPA Coordinate with faculty and staff to help meet students’ academic needs Connect at-risk students with appropriate academic support programming Collect, document, and provide necessary reports related to departmental goals Other duties as assigned by the Director Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree, 2-3 years of experience in higher education, student affairs, counseling, or other closely related field; • Strong time management and problem solving skills • Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite • Excellent written and communication skills • Ability to communicate with a variety of campus constituencies Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling, or other closely related field is preferred. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/110": {
      "title": "Career Specialist",
      "description": "Career Specialist. Department: S3C. Full-Time. The Career Specialist is an entry level position that guides students through career exploration, helps prepare students for work-based learning and internship opportunities, and assists with job searches and graduate school processes. Job Duties: Career Advising Facilitate individual and group career exploration to students, including assessment of interests, values, skills, and career pathways. Facilitate opportunities for students to explore strengths, interests, and potential career directions through structured experiences and activities. Assist students in preparing for work-based learning experiences, internships, employment, and graduate or professional programs. Assist students in preparing their personal documents for job searches or graduate applications. Support development of career readiness skills, including communication, professionalism, and job search strategies. Career Services Program Development Assist in the development and implementation of EDGE programming. Assist in the development of partnerships with university and community stakeholders. Assist the Director of the Center with long-range goals in the program area. Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree in counseling, student services administration, higher education, human resources or related field from an accredited institution (experience in higher education and/or Master’s degree preferred); Skills and Knowledge: Excellent communication, organizational and time management, problem solving and decision making, and customer service skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office suite and other office and record-keeping systems. Experience : Previous experience in college career services or similar experience in career development in a business environment (preferred). License/Certification: Professional certification in career development (e.g., NCDA, GCDF) or related area preferred. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/93": {
      "title": "Work Study - Fall '26 - CORE Program Office Assistant",
      "description": "Work Study - Fall '26 - CORE Program Office Assistant. Department: S3C. Part-Time. Position Description: The CORE Office Assistant serves as the first point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and visitors entering the Success Coaching Office. This position provides administrative support, assists with daily office operations, helps maintain a welcoming environment, and supports student engagement through social media and promotional efforts. The ideal candidate is friendly, organized, dependable, and passionate about helping fellow students succeed. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Greet students, faculty, staff, and visitors in a professional and welcoming manner, assisting students with check-in procedures for coaching appointments and events. Answer basic questions about campus services and direct students to appropriate resources. Assist with preparation, planning, and promoting events and assisting CORE staff during events and special projects as assigned. Develop graphics, photos, videos, and student-focused posts that promote student success resources, and assist in creating content for the office’s social media platforms. This position requires a commitment of 10 hours per week, including designated office hours. The ideal candidate is comfortable working independently as well as collaborating with campus partners and other students and will foster belonging and serve others through their work. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/62": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach - Wrestling",
      "description": "Assistant Coach - Wrestling. Department: Wrestling. Part-Time. The Assistant Wrestling Coach supports the Head Wrestling Coach in all aspects of administering a competitive NCAA Division III wrestling program. This role helps foster student-athlete development, competitive success, academic achievement, and adherence to institutional and conference expectations. The coach assists in planning practices, recruitment, match preparation, program operations, and building a positive team culture aligned with the university’s mission. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Coaching & Player Development Assist with planning, organizing, and conducting daily practices and training sessions. Provide technical instruction, skill development, and individualized coaching for student-athletes. Support scouting of opponents and match strategy preparation. Promote a culture of sportsmanship, discipline, accountability, and continuous improvement. Recruitment Identify, evaluate, and recruit prospective student-athletes who align with academic and athletic standards of the institution. Maintain communication with high school coaches, club coaches, and prospective students. Participate in on-campus recruiting visits and off-campus recruiting events. Ensure all recruiting activities comply with NCAA Division III rules. Program Administration Assist with scheduling, travel logistics, budgeting support, and equipment management. Contribute to program compliance, including roster management, eligibility protocols, and required reporting. Support fundraising initiatives, alumni engagement, and community outreach events. Student-Athlete Support Encourage academic success through mentoring and collaboration with campus resources. Promote well-being, injury prevention, and responsible decision-making among student athletes. Model inclusive and supportive behavior reflects institutional values. Other Duties Represent the university at athletics department meetings, campus events, and conference functions as needed. Other responsibilities as assigned by the Head Wrestling Coach or Athletics Director. Required Some Education Strong understanding of wrestling techniques, training methods, and match strategy. Ability to recruit effectively within NCAA Division III guidelines. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Commitment to the academic and personal development of student-athletes. Preferred Knowledge of strength and conditioning principles. Familiarity with NCAA Division III compliance expectations. CPR/First Aid certification. Bachelor’s degree. Minimum Required Education: Some education or bachelor's degree Work Environment & Physical Requirements Frequent evening and weekend commitments. Travel for competitions and recruiting. Ability to demonstrate wrestling techniques and conduct physically active training sessions. Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/118": {
      "title": "Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Student Ambassador. Department: Admissions. Part-Time. The office of Admission is seeking Student Ambassadors to assist with recruiting and enrollment. Job Duties • Conduct campus visits and virtual campus tours. • Communicate with prospective students via in person, phone, text, email, mail, etc. • Create personalized videos for admitted students. • Provide coverage of front desk and main phone line. • Assemble information packets for mailing. • Assist with on-campus or virtual events. • Some evening and Saturday work may be required. • Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications High School/G.E.D. Must be a current McMurry student Preferred Qualifications •Computer knowledge. •Team player, fast learner, and strong work ethic. •Appropriately dressed in business casual or professional attire. Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/121": {
      "title": "Sports Information Assistant - Part Time",
      "description": "Sports Information Assistant - Part Time. Department: Athletics SID. Part-Time. Major/Essential Duties of the Job: Coordinate and produce all live video streaming for home sporting events at various venues on campus Experience with NCAA live stats and Presto stats. Assist in keeping statistics, maintaining program records, and tracking statistics for teams. Assist in all daily operations of the Sports Information office, working under the Director of Sports Information. Assume other projects and duties as assigned and agreed upon by the Sports Information Director and Athletics Director. Maintain and oversee athletics media and game day equipment and manage post-event reporting and documentation requirements. Coordinate department photography and videography, including headshots, team photos, media day, promo videos, and game day action photos Help with creating and managing content (photography, videography, and graphics) for the McMurry Athletics social media portfolio (Instagram, Facebook, X) Assist in writing post-game recaps for select sports. Assist with the recruitment, training, scheduling, and supervision of student workers/assistants. Support special athletic events, including the Wally Award ceremony, Jimmy Lee Pierce Golf Classic, and other events as directed by the Athletics Director and Sports Information Director. Preferred Education/Experience: Bachelor’s degree in Sports Management, Communications, Journalism, or a related field. 1-2 years of experience in sports information, media relations, broadcasting, or a related role. Proficiency with video and live stream equipment and photography EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/120": {
      "title": "Work Study - Fall/Spring '26/'27 Post Office Student Worker",
      "description": "Work Study - Fall/Spring '26/'27 Post Office Student Worker. Department: Post Office. Part-Time. Job Duties: Greet and assist visitors. Help put up mail. Write up and deliver packages, paper, print supplies. Run errands on campus. Required Qualifications: Applicant must be enrolled in summer semester classes. Preferred Qualifications: Candidate must have good customer service skills, detail oriented, and the ability to accurately handle mail. Must be dependable, responsible, honest and able to adhere to confidentially according to departmental standards. Physical Demands: This position requires heavy lifting at times. Special Conditions for Eligibility: This position is for McMurry Students who are enrolled in classes in the semesters during which they wish to work. Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action: McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy."
    }
